  "text": "To solve the problem, we will use coordinate geometry and properties of right-angled triangles. We achieve this by following the steps below:\n\n1. Establish a coordinate system for the points involved in the right triangle.\n2. Apply the given lengths and relationships to find the coordinates of points \\(A\\), \\(B\\), \\(C\\), \\(D\\), \\(E\\), and \\(F\\).\n3. Use these coordinates to calculate the desired length \\(FD\\).\n\n### Step 1: Coordinate System Setup\nWe position the right triangle \\(\\triangle ABC\\) such that:\n- \\(A\\) is at the origin \\((0, 0)\\).\n- \\(B\\) is at \\((0, 45)\\) since \\(AB = 45\\).\n- \\(C\\) is at \\((45, 0)\\) since \\(AC\\) is the hypotenuse and \\(\\angle B = 90^\\circ\\).\n\n### Step 2: Identify Coordinates of \\(D\\), \\(E\\), \\(B\\), and \\(F\\)\nGiven:\n- \\(AB = 45\\) \n- \\(BE = 15\\)\n- \\(\\angle ADB = 90^\\circ\\)\n\n#### Calculating the Coordinates of \\(E\\):\nSince \\(BE = 15\\), and \\(B\\) is at \\((0, 45)\\), we find \\(E\\) by moving horizontally from \\((0, 45)\\):\n\\[ E = (0, 45 - 15) = (0, 30) \\]\n\n#### Calculating the Coordinates of \\(D\\):\nGiven \\(D\\) lies on \\(AC\\), we know \\(AC\\) has endpoints \\((0, 45)\\) and \\((45, 0)\\):\n\\[ D = (15, 15) \\]\nThis is why \\(D\\) coordinates are calculated as such since it bisects \\(AB\\) and evenly splits \\(AC\\).\n\n#### Calculating the Coordinates of \\(B\\) and \\(F\\):\nSince \\(\\angle BED = 90^\\circ\\) and \\(\\overline{BF}\\) is the angle bisector of \\(\\angle EBD\\), we position \\(F\\) on \\(AB\\) such that:\n- \\(AF = 32\\)\nThus:\n\\[ F = (32, 0) \\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate \\(FD\\)\nWe can now calculate \\(FD\\) using the distance formula:\n\\[ FD = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2} \\]\nwhere \\((x_1, y_1)\\) are coordinates of \\(F\\) and \\((x_2, y_2)\\) are coordinates of \\(D\\).\n\nPertaining to the coordinates we derived:\n\\[ F = (32, 0) \\]\n\\[ D = (15, 15) \\]\n\nNow we apply the distance formula:\n\\[ FD = \\sqrt{(32 - 15)^2 + (0 - 15)^2} \\]\n\\[ FD = \\sqrt{(17)^2 + (-15)^2} \\]\n\\[ FD = \\sqrt{289 + 225} \\]\n\\[ FD = \\sqrt{514} \\]\n\\[ FD = 3 \\sqrt{53} \\]\n\nThus, the length \\(FD\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{3\\sqrt{53}}\n\\]",
